# Deliberately narrow to high-signal categories: bugprone/clang-analyzer catch
# actual bugs, performance flags real waste. modernize/readability/
# cppcoreguidelines were tried against this codebase and mostly fight its
# existing (intentional) style — e.g. brace-less single-line ifs, short loop
# variable names — rather than find defects, so they're left out rather than
# fought check-by-check.
#
# clang-analyzer-cplusplus.NewDeleteLeaks is further excluded: every
# QMetaObject::invokeMethod(obj, lambda, Qt::QueuedConnection) call (used in
# main.cpp and MpvPlayer.cpp) trips it. Qt allocates a slot-object to own the
# functor and frees it itself once the queued call runs, but the analyzer
# can't see across that ownership transfer and reports a "leak" anchored
# inside <QtCore/qobjectdefs.h>, not at the call site — a NOLINT in our own
# code wouldn't even land on the right line. Well-known Qt + clang-analyzer
# friction, not something specific to this codebase.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -portability-avoid-pragma-once,
  -clang-analyzer-cplusplus.NewDeleteLeaks

WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '(^|[/\\])src[/\\].*'
FormatStyle: none
